// Hexproof [CR#702.11b]: "can't be the target of spells or abilities your
// opponents control". The `from` param narrows it to matching sources
// [CR#702.11d] via the deed agent's SOURCE arm — "[quality] spells your
// opponents control or abilities your opponents control from [quality]
// sources" is ONE row: the opponent clause judges the stack object, the
// quality its source (a spell is itself a source [CR#609.7a]; an ability's
// source is its generator [CR#113.7]). "hexproof from [quality]" IS a
// hexproof ability, so a "lose hexproof" effect [CR#702.11e] strips it too;
// hence one macro, one `Composite(name: "Hexproof")` identity. The optional
// `${ from #from#}` fragment carries the parameterized printing; bare
// `Hexproof()` renders just "hexproof". Player-proxy carriers get
// [CR#702.11c] for free.
(
    name: "Hexproof",
    template: "hexproof${ from #from#}",
    kinds: [KeywordAbility],
    params: { "from": Default(Filter, Any) },
    body: Composite(
        name: "Hexproof",
        abilities: [Static(Cant(Target(
                on: Ref(This),
                by: (
                    stack_object: ControlledBy(OpponentOf(Ref(You))),
                    source: Param(from),
                ),
            )))],
    ),
)